# Hotmart checkout — what to create there, and what to paste back here
#
# Ash decided on 8 Aug 2026 that Hotmart takes every market, and on 9 Aug 2026
# that Stripe is abandoned altogether. Hotmart is the only checkout: the front
# end builds pay.hotmart.com links and there is no other processor to fall back
# to. VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT is therefore no longer a switch, it is a
# requirement — with it empty every buy button on the site is dead.
#
# These are build-time variables. Vite bakes them into the bundle, so changing
# one means rebuilding and redeploying, not restarting the server. Nothing here
# is a secret: every value ends up visible in a checkout URL anyway.
#
# VITE_CHECKOUT_PROVIDER and VITE_HOTMART_LOCALES used to live here. They chose
# between two processors and there is only one now, so the code no longer reads
# them. Leaving them set does nothing.
#
# The ladder these codes belong to: marketing/flu143-esteira-hotmart.md

# The product id in the checkout URL: pay.hotmart.com/<this>
# REQUIRED. Nothing on the site can be bought without it.
#
# This one is product 1, the protocol, and it carries the five offers below it.
# The other rungs are separate products in the panel — they have to be, an order
# bump can only attach one product to another product's checkout — so each has
# its own id and its own line further down. Pairing a rung's offer code with
# product 1's id does not sell that rung: Hotmart redirects to
# /error?errorMessage=008.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT=

# Rung 1, the platform, 27 EUR. A Hotmart order bump is fixed per offer, so the
# same product is published four times, once per sleep type, each with the bump
# headline that matches what the visitor just answered in the quiz. Create all
# four; the generic one below is the fallback for anyone who arrives without a
# quiz result, and it is the only one strictly required.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_MAINTENANCE=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_ONSET=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_MIXED=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_CIRCADIAN=

# Rung 2, Recovery Pack, +19 EUR. Attached as the order bump on the four offers
# above. The offer code is what the webhook reads off the notification to know
# the pack was bought. The product id is only needed to sell the pack on its
# own, which is what /upgrade does for buyers who said no at the checkout and
# come back for it later; leave it empty and that page shows its unavailable
# copy instead of linking to Hotmart's error screen.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_BUMP=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_BUMP=

# Rung 3, the 3AM Relapse Kit, 47 EUR, one click after the purchase clears.
# Still being written. Leave empty until it is, or buyers pay for nothing.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_OTO1=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_OTO1=

# Rung 4, a single protocol, 9 EUR, shown only to whoever declines rung 3.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_DOWNSELL=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_DOWNSELL=

# Rung 5, a second seat for the partner who gets woken up too, 17 EUR.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_SEAT=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_SEAT=

# Rung 6, Reset Season, 39 EUR for the year, paid once. Not a subscription:
# the sales page promises no subscription, and that has to stay true in the
# panel as well. Create it as a one-off product with a yearly delivery, never
# as a recurring plan.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_SEASON=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_SEASON=

# Rung 7, personal recalibration read off the buyer's own sleep log, 79 to 149.
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT_BACKEND=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_BACKEND=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE SERVER HALF. These do NOT go in this file.
#
# Everything above is baked into the browser bundle at build time. What follows
# is read by the API at runtime and belongs in the root .env, the one systemd
# hands to sleepwired-api.service. One of them is a secret, which is reason
# enough for the two halves to live apart.
#
# After editing the root .env:  sudo systemctl restart sleepwired-api
#
#   HOTMART_HOTTOK=<the token from Ferramentas → Webhook (API e notificações)>
#
# The webhook URL to register in that same panel screen, for the events
# PURCHASE_APPROVED, PURCHASE_COMPLETE, PURCHASE_REFUNDED and PURCHASE_CHARGEBACK:
#
#   https://sleepwired.com/api/hotmart/webhook
#
# The offer codes do not need repeating: the server reads HOTMART_OFF_FRONT and
# falls back to VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT, so pasting each code once into the root
# .env feeds both halves. Optional, and worth setting once the products exist:
# the product ucodes, which keep delivery working if somebody creates an offer
# in the panel and forgets to paste its code back here.
#
#   HOTMART_UCODE_FRONT=      HOTMART_UCODE_BUMP=       HOTMART_UCODE_OTO1=
#   HOTMART_UCODE_DOWNSELL=   HOTMART_UCODE_SEAT=
#
# With HOTMART_HOTTOK unset the webhook answers 503 and grants nothing, which is
# the same safety net VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT gives the front end.
